 "differences": {
  "totalSDps": {
   "expected": 96.39597,
   "cause": "Coriolis changed its sustained dps formula after this export: Ship.js (2017) spread a clip over clip/rof + reload seconds; Module.getSustainedFactor now uses (clip - 1)/rof + reload, as the last shot needs no interval. Also the medium turreted cannon fires every 2.5 s (rof 0.4) where 2017 data had rof 0.405. Today: plasma accelerator (dps 31.3, rof 0.25, clip 5, reload 6) 31.3 x (5 / (4/0.25 + 6)) / 0.25 = 28.454545; two cannons (dps 7.908, rof 0.4, clip 5, reload 4) 7.908 x (5 / (4/0.4 + 4)) / 0.4 = 7.060714 each; beams 3 x 14.34 + 2 x 5.4 (no clip). Sum 96.39597. With the 2017 formula the plasma accelerator gives 24.0769, which is Coriolis's 14.45 absolute / 0.6."
  },
  "totalAbsSDps": {
   "expected": 17.07273,
   "cause": "Sustained formula change (see totalSDps): 0.6 x 28.454545."
  },
  "totalKinSDps": {
   "expected": 19.81234,
   "cause": "Sustained formula change and cannon rate of fire (see totalSDps): 0.2 x 28.454545 + 2 x 7.060714."
  }
 },
